# Site facts for the two-Spark pair. Copy to launcher/hosts.env on both nodes (same recipe path on both) and edit.
# Every address here is an EXAMPLE. Plain KEY=VALUE lines; a variable already set in the environment wins.
#
# Cabling: one QSFP cable between the two Sparks' ConnectX-7 port 0. Each port is two PCIe x4 halves, each with its
# own RoCE function and netdev (rocep1s0f0 / enp1s0f0np0 and roceP2p1s0f0 / enP2p1s0f0np0 on a DGX Spark); give each
# half its own /24 on both nodes. RoCE v2 over IPv4 must sit at GID index 3 on both halves (GID_INDEX).

# Fabric (rail 1) addresses: torch.distributed master (rank 0), gloo and NCCL bootstrap, VLLM_HOST_IP.
RANK0_FABRIC_IP=10.100.1.1
RANK1_FABRIC_IP=10.100.1.2
# Interface of rail 1 (NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME / GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME).
FABRIC_IFNAME=enp1s0f0np0
# The two RoCE functions of the cabled port, rail 1 first.
HCAS=rocep1s0f0,roceP2p1s0f0
# One ping per rail, from rank 0 to rank 1's address on that rail: "<rail>:<ip>". pair-up.sh fails closed if rail 1
# is down and falls back to rail 1 only (RoCEnante off) if rail 2 is down.
LINK_CHECKS="1:10.100.1.2 2:10.100.2.2"

# ssh target pair-up.sh uses from rank 0 (default: [SSH_USER@]RANK1_FABRIC_IP). Key-based, non-interactive
# (BatchMode) ssh from rank 0 to rank 1 is required.
SSH_USER=
#RANK1_SSH=user@192.0.2.12

# The serving view (view/build-view.sh output), identical on both nodes.
VIEW=/srv/models/CYBER-FROST-3.8-NVFP4-V2-serving
# API keys, one per line, readable by the docker user. Must exist on both nodes: both ranks parse the same command
# line, although only rank 0 serves HTTP. Bind-mounted read-only and read at exec time, so no key appears in
# `docker inspect`.
API_KEY_FILE=/etc/cyberfrost/api-keys
# b12x checkouts live at $B12X_ROOT/<short sha> (the profile's B12X=e4084d2e -> $HOME/b12x/e4084d2e).
B12X_ROOT=$HOME/b12x
# Per-rank state: vLLM / FlashInfer / b12x caches, memory-guard state and log.
STATE=$HOME/vllm-cyberfrost-state
# Optional: pin the container to cores (we use the ten Cortex-X925 cores of each GB10: CPUSET=5-9,15-19).
#CPUSET=5-9,15-19
